  None of these repositories ships a NOTICE file.

======================================================================
3. Logic ported (reimplemented in Python, no source lines copied)
======================================================================

The parser reads command lines the way each tool does. Where that meant following a
tool's own code, the logic was rewritten in Python. These are listed so the origin
of the behaviour is clear.

Helm (https://github.com/helm/helm), pkg/strvals: --set/--set-string/--set-json
  value parsing and typedVal. Copyright The Helm Authors. Apache-2.0.

Go standard library (https://go.dev), strconv ParseInt (base 0), ParseFloat,
  ParseBool, and time.ParseDuration. Copyright 2009 The Go Authors.
  BSD-3-Clause (text below).

spf13/pflag (https://github.com/spf13/pflag): flag syntax, short-letter groups,
  value types (StringSlice CSV splitting, StringArray, StringToString, Count).
  Copyright (c) 2012 Alex Ogier, Copyright (c) 2012 The Go Authors.
  BSD-3-Clause (text below).

kubectl and cli-runtime (https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes): argument
  handling per verb (for example logs.go Complete). The Kubernetes Authors.
  Apache-2.0.

aws-cli (version 2.37.4), awscli/argprocess.py and awscli/paramfile.py: how a value
  is unpacked as JSON or shorthand and when it is read from a file.
  Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. Apache-2.0.

Google Cloud SDK, googlecloudsdk/calliope/arg_parsers.py and
  googlecloudsdk/core/util/iso_duration.py: ArgList, ArgDict, BinarySize,
  Duration, Boolean and the ^DELIM^ syntax. Copyright Google LLC. Apache-2.0.

azure-cli (https://github.com/Azure/azure-cli): validate_tags,
  get_three_state_flag, get_enum_type. Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.
  MIT License (text below).

knack (https://github.com/microsoft/knack): @file argument preprocessing.
  Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. MIT License (text below).

GitHub CLI (https://github.com/cli/cli): gh api field and host handling.
  Copyright (c) 2019 GitHub Inc. MIT License (text below).

git (https://git-scm.com): which refspecs a push builds, branch and tag filter
  options, parse-options abbreviation rules. git is licensed under GPL-2.0. No git
  source is included: the behaviour was reimplemented in Python, with git's
  documentation and source (builtin/push.c, builtin/branch.c, builtin/tag.c,
  parse-options.c) used as a reference for what git does.

